<!--
  Geofence Reminder — iOS Info.plist Usage Description Keys

  Add these entries to ios/GeofenceReminder/Info.plist inside the <dict> tag:

  <key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
  <string>We need your location to create geofence reminders. Your location is only used when the app is open and for monitoring nearby areas.</string>

  <key>NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
  <string>We need your location to monitor geofence boundaries even when the app is in the background. You will be notified when you enter or leave a saved area.</string>

  For iOS 13+, "Always" authorization requires the following key in Info.plist:
  <key>NSLocationAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
  <string>We need your location to monitor geofence boundaries in the background. You will receive notifications when entering saved areas.</string>

  Note: iOS requires both "When In Use" and "Always" usage descriptions.
  The app must call CLLocationManager.requestAlwaysAuthorization() to trigger
  the "Always" permission prompt. Without this, background monitoring will fail.

  Also ensure these capabilities are enabled in Xcode:
  - Background Modes: Location updates
  - Capabilities: Background fetch (optional, for background notification delivery)
-->
